  "problem": "A sample ${X}_{1},{X}_{2},…,{X}_{12}$ is drawn from a population with population mean $\\mu $ and population variance ${\\sigma }^{2}.$ If $\\mu $ and $\\sigma $ are both  known, which of the following are statistics?\n\nI. ${\\sum }_{i=1}^{12}|{X}_{i}-\\mu |$\n\nII. ${\\sum }_{i=1}^{12}({X}_{i}+\\sigma )$\n\nIII. $min({X}_{1},{X}_{2},…,{X}_{12})$",
